0..70 Comment "// Order through the prelude\'s `Ord`: `<`, `<=`, `>` and `>=` call the"
71..145 Comment "// prelude\'s `lt`, `le`, `gt` and `ge`, whose model of `Ord` the operands\'"
146..214 Comment "// type resolves. `OrdInteger` answers the integers with the integer"
215..292 Comment "// primitives, so their verdicts are the primitives\'; `OrdString` answers the"
293..368 Comment "// strings byte by byte, the order a Rust `BTreeMap<String, _>` keeps. Each"
369..428 Comment "// includes its `Eq` model, so `==` still resolves at both."
429..431 Comment "//"
432..447 Comment "// - see: #2333"
